---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const EMAIL = 'info.oneskillstudio@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Training & Support"
  description="Oracle HCM Cloud training and technical support — Fast Formula, Absence Management, Time and Labor, HDL, Benefits. Delivered by an Oracle ACE Associate with a decade of APAC implementations."
>
  <div class="tr">

    <!-- ══════════ INTRO BAND ══════════ -->
    <section class="tr-shell">
      <div class="band">
        <div class="band-grid">
          <div>
            <div class="tr-eyebrow">Training &amp; Support</div>
            <h1>Work through it with someone who has shipped it</h1>
            <p class="lead">
              Most Oracle HCM problems aren't knowledge gaps — they're the specific,
              undocumented behaviour of one feature under one configuration. I help teams
              get past those, either by teaching the underlying model or by working the
              actual problem with you.
            </p>
            <a class="cta" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>
              <span class="cta-ico" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m2 7 10 6 10-6"/></svg>
              </span>
              <span>
                <b>{EMAIL}</b>
                <em>Tell me the module and the symptom — that's enough to start.</em>
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>

          <aside class="cred">
            <div class="cred-row"><b>10+</b><span>years on Oracle HCM Cloud</span></div>
            <div class="cred-row"><b>6</b><span>APAC markets delivered</span></div>
            <div class="cred-row"><b>ACE</b><span>Oracle ACE Associate · AIOUG</span></div>
            <div class="cred-note">
              Everything below comes out of live production rollouts, not courseware.
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ TRAINING ══════════ -->
    <section class="tr-shell sec">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-kicker">Training</div>
        <h2>Learn the model, not the clicks</h2>
        <p class="sec-lead">
          Sessions are built around real formulas, real data and real integrations, and they
          assume you'll be maintaining what you write. Delivered remotely, recorded if you
          want it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="track">Fast Formula &amp; functional</div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Fast Formula</div>
          <h3>Fast Formula, properly</h3>
          <p>
            Contexts, database items, routes and the seven building blocks. Why there is no
            null, what <code>DEFAULT</code> actually protects against, and how to read a
            compilation error.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Time &amp; Labor</div>
          <h3>TER and TCR frameworks</h3>
          <p>
            The input contract, marker rows, parallel arrays, and the state machines behind
            continuous-hours and overtime rules. Built from a production formula, traced
            line by line.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Absence</div>
          <h3>Accrual design</h3>
          <p>
            Matrix formulas, accrual bands, carryover and ceiling behaviour, and the
            multi-country leave patterns that come up across APAC rollouts.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">HDL</div>
          <h3>Transformation formulas</h3>
          <p>
            OPERATION routing, METADATA arrays, LINEREPEATNO passes and WSA caching —
            including where WSA is a correctness requirement rather than an optimisation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Benefits</div>
          <h3>Eligibility &amp; rates</h3>
          <p>
            Post Election Edit validation, cross-plan dependencies, rate periodization, and
            reading enrollment at a future effective date.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Debugging</div>
          <h3>Making formulas talk</h3>
          <p>
            Logging idioms for every formula type, the profile options that silently discard
            output, and where each module actually writes its log.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="track">Reporting, data &amp; integration</div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">HDL</div>
          <h3>HCM Data Loader</h3>
          <p>
            File structure, business objects and discriminators, SourceSystemId and MERGE
            behaviour, and reading the error log well enough to fix a failed load without
            guessing.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">BI Publisher</div>
          <h3>BI Publisher reporting</h3>
          <p>
            Data models and SQL against the HCM schema, bursting, layout templates, secured
            list views, and scheduling reports that keep working after a release.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">OTBI</div>
          <h3>OTBI analytics</h3>
          <p>
            Subject areas and how they join, folder and attribute selection, filters and
            prompts, and where OTBI is the right tool versus where you should drop to BI
            Publisher.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">SQL</div>
          <h3>SQL for HCM</h3>
          <p>
            Practical SQL against the HCM tables — joins, analytic functions, date-effective
            rows and the <code>_F</code> table patterns that trip people up on their first
            extract.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">OIC</div>
          <h3>Oracle Integration Cloud</h3>
          <p>
            Integration patterns for HCM — adapters, mappings, scheduled versus event-driven
            flows, error handling and retries, and moving files in and out reliably.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">End to end</div>
          <h3>Putting it together</h3>
          <p>
            One realistic requirement carried through the whole stack: extract with SQL,
            report in BI Publisher, load with HDL, integrate with OIC. This is where the
            pieces stop feeling separate.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ INTERVIEW PREP ══════════ -->
    <section class="tr-shell sec" id="interview">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-kicker">Interview preparation</div>
        <h2>Built around the questions that actually get asked</h2>
        <p class="sec-lead">
          Oracle HCM interviews rarely test definitions. They test whether you've hit the
          problem before — and whether you can explain what you did about it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prep">
        <article class="prep-card">
          <h3>Module-by-module coverage</h3>
          <p>
            Fast Formula, HDL, BI Publisher, OTBI, SQL and OIC — the questions that come up
            for each, and the follow-ups that come after your first answer.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="prep-card">
          <h3>Scenario questions</h3>
          <p>
            "A load failed for 200 of 5,000 rows — what do you check first?" The kind of
            question where a memorised answer falls apart on the second sentence.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="prep-card">
          <h3>Mock interviews</h3>
          <p>
            Live, timed, with honest feedback afterwards on what was weak — including when
            the problem is delivery rather than knowledge.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="prep-card">
          <h3>Your own project, explained</h3>
          <p>
            Most candidates lose points describing work they genuinely did. We rehearse
            your actual rollouts into answers you can give under pressure.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="prep-note">
        <b>On outcomes.</b> I'll prepare you thoroughly and tell you honestly when you're
        ready — but hiring decisions involve headcount, budget, timing and competition that
        neither of us controls. What I can commit to is that you'll walk in knowing your
        material, and that we keep working until you do.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ SUPPORT ══════════ -->
    <section class="tr-shell sec">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-kicker">Support</div>
        <h2>Or bring me the problem</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="rows">
        <article class="row">
          <span class="row-n">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Formula review</h3>
            <p>
              You have something that compiles and mostly works. I read it and tell you where
              it breaks — the unguarded array read, the case-sensitive comparison, the missing
              reset that only shows up on a multi-day timecard.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="row">
          <span class="row-n">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Live debugging</h3>
            <p>
              Something works in test and fails in production, or works for most people and
              fails for a few. We work it together against your actual data and logs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="row">
          <span class="row-n">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Design review</h3>
            <p>
              Before you build. Whether the rule belongs in configuration, a TER, a TCR or a
              workflow — and what a second country will do to the design you're about to
              commit to.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="row">
          <span class="row-n">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Second opinion</h3>
            <p>
              A short, honest read on an approach someone has proposed — including when the
              answer is that it's fine and you should proceed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ CONTACT ══════════ -->
    <section class="tr-shell sec sec--last">
      <div class="contact">
        <div>
          <h3>Start with an email</h3>
          <p>
            Include the module, what you expected, and what actually happened. If there's a
            formula or a log extract, paste it — it saves a round trip.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="clink" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
      </div>

      <p class="note">
        Availability varies with client commitments, so response times aren't guaranteed.
        Views on this site are personal and not those of any employer or client. Oracle and
        the Oracle product names referenced are trademarks of Oracle Corporation.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Scoped under .tr; class names prefixed where global.css already owns them. */
  .tr{
    --tr-bg:#FDF6EE; --tr-surface:#FFFFFF; --tr-surface-2:#F7EFE4;
    --tr-line:#E6DACA; --tr-line-soft:#EFE6D9;
    --tr-navy:#003060; --tr-ink:#0A2A4A; --tr-dim:#56687E; --tr-faint:#637181;
    --tr-blue:#184878; --tr-blue-lift:#186090;
    --tr-orange:#F07818; --tr-orange-dp:#B75107;
    --tr-orange-wash:rgba(240,120,24,.09); --tr-orange-edge:rgba(240,120,24,.42);
    --tr-f:Verdana, Geneva, 'DejaVu Sans', sans-serif;

    background:var(--tr-bg); color:var(--tr-ink);
    font-family:var(--tr-f); font-size:15px; line-height:1.72;
    padding-block:26px 8px;
  }
  .tr *{box-sizing:border-box}
  .tr-shell{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}

  /* ── band ── */
  .band{
    position:relative;margin:0 0 40px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(70% 120% at 92% 14%, rgba(24,72,120,.05), transparent 58%),
      linear-gradient(180deg,#FFFCF8 0%, var(--tr-surface-2) 100%);
    border:1px solid var(--tr-line);border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;
  }
  .band::before{
    content:'';position:absolute;inset:0 0 auto 0;height:3px;
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--tr-navy) 0%, var(--tr-blue-lift) 46%, var(--tr-orange) 100%);
  }
  .band-grid{
    display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(0,1fr);
    gap:36px;align-items:start;padding:36px 34px 34px;
  }
  .tr-eyebrow{
    background:none;padding:0;border-radius:0;   /* beat global .eyebrow pill */
    font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--tr-orange-dp);margin-bottom:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;
  }
  .tr-eyebrow::after{
    content:'';height:2px;flex:1;max-width:120px;border-radius:2px;
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--tr-orange),transparent);
  }
  .tr h1{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-weight:700;
    font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.3rem);
    line-height:1.14;letter-spacing:-.036em;color:var(--tr-navy);margin:0 0 16px;
  }
  .lead{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--tr-dim);margin:0 0 24px;max-width:58ch}

  .cta{
    display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;text-decoration:none;
    background:var(--tr-surface);border:1px solid var(--tr-line);
    border-left:3px solid var(--tr-orange);border-radius:10px;
    padding:14px 18px;
    box-shadow:0 2px 4px rgba(10,42,74,.04), 0 12px 28px -20px rgba(10,42,74,.26);
    transition:border-color .2s ease,transform .2s ease;
  }
  .cta:hover{border-color:var(--tr-orange-edge);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .cta-ico{
    width:34px;height:34px;flex-shrink:0;border-radius:8px;
    background:var(--tr-navy);color:var(--tr-orange);
    display:grid;place-items:center;
  }
  .cta-ico svg{width:17px;height:17px}
  .cta b{display:block;font-size:13px;color:var(--tr-navy);letter-spacing:-.01em;word-break:break-all}
  .cta em{display:block;font-style:normal;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--tr-faint);margin-top:2px}

  .cred{
    background:var(--tr-surface);border:1px solid var(--tr-line);
    border-radius:12px;padding:18px 20px;
  }
  .cred-row{
    display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;
    padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--tr-line-soft);
  }
  .cred-row:last-of-type{border-bottom:none}
  .cred-row b{
    font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:var(--tr-navy);
    letter-spacing:-.03em;min-width:44px;
  }
  .cred-row span{font-size:11px;color:var(--tr-dim);line-height:1.5}
  .cred-note{
    margin-top:12px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--tr-line-soft);
    font-size:10.5px;color:var(--tr-faint);line-height:1.6;font-style:italic;
  }

  /* ── sections ── */
  .sec{padding-bottom:46px}
  .sec--last{padding-bottom:20px}
  .sec-head{margin-bottom:22px}
  .sec-kicker{
    font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--tr-orange-dp);margin-bottom:8px;
  }
  .tr h2{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-weight:700;
    font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.3vw,1.7rem);
    letter-spacing:-.032em;color:var(--tr-navy);line-height:1.2;margin:0;
  }
  .sec-lead{font-size:14px;color:var(--tr-dim);max-width:64ch;margin:12px 0 0}

  /* ── training cards ── */
  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px}
  .tr .card{
    position:relative;background:var(--tr-surface);border:1px solid var(--tr-line);
    border-radius:12px;padding:20px;overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(10,42,74,.03);
    transition:border-color .2s ease,transform .2s ease,box-shadow .2s ease;
  }
  .tr .card:hover{
    border-color:var(--tr-orange-edge);transform:translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow:0 2px 4px rgba(10,42,74,.04), 0 16px 34px -20px rgba(10,42,74,.26);
  }
  .tr .card::after{
    content:'';position:absolute;inset:0 0 auto 0;height:3px;
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--tr-navy),var(--tr-orange));
    opacity:0;transition:opacity .2s ease;
  }
  .tr .card:hover::after{opacity:1}
  .card-tag{
    font-size:9px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--tr-orange-dp);margin-bottom:10px;
  }
  .tr .card h3{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--tr-navy);
    letter-spacing:-.026em;margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.3;
  }
  .tr .card p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--tr-dim);line-height:1.62;margin:0}
  .tr .card code{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;
    color:var(--tr-orange-dp);background:var(--tr-orange-wash);
    padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:-.02em;
  }

  /* ── track label ── */
  .track{
    font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--tr-navy);margin:0 0 12px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;
  }
  .track:not(:first-of-type){margin-top:26px}
  .track::after{
    content:'';height:1px;flex:1;background:var(--tr-line);
  }

  /* ── interview prep ── */
  .prep{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:14px}
  .prep-card{
    background:var(--tr-surface);border:1px solid var(--tr-line);
    border-left:3px solid var(--tr-blue);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 20px;
    transition:border-color .2s ease,transform .2s ease;
  }
  .prep-card:hover{border-color:var(--tr-orange-edge);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .tr .prep-card h3{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--tr-navy);
    letter-spacing:-.024em;margin:0 0 6px;
  }
  .prep-card p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--tr-dim);line-height:1.62;margin:0}
  .prep-note{
    margin-top:16px;background:var(--tr-surface-2);
    border:1px solid var(--tr-line);border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px;
    font-size:12.5px;color:var(--tr-dim);line-height:1.68;
  }
  .prep-note b{color:var(--tr-navy);font-weight:700}

  /* ── support rows ── */
  .rows{display:grid;gap:12px}
  .row{
    display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:flex-start;
    background:var(--tr-surface);border:1px solid var(--tr-line);
    border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;
    transition:border-color .2s ease,transform .2s ease;
  }
  .row:hover{border-color:var(--tr-orange-edge);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .row-n{
    font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:var(--tr-orange);
    letter-spacing:-.02em;flex-shrink:0;min-width:26px;line-height:1.5;
  }
  .tr .row h3{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--tr-navy);
    letter-spacing:-.024em;margin:0 0 5px;
  }
  .row p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--tr-dim);line-height:1.62;margin:0;max-width:80ch}

  /* ── contact ── */
  .contact{
    display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;
    background:var(--tr-navy);border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;margin-bottom:30px;
  }
  .tr .contact h3{
    font-family:var(--tr-f);font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;
    letter-spacing:-.026em;margin:0 0 5px;
  }
  .contact p{font-size:12.5px;color:#A8C0D8;margin:0;max-width:62ch;line-height:1.6}
  .tr .clink{
    font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.01em;
    padding:11px 20px;border-radius:999px;text-decoration:none;
    background:var(--tr-orange);color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;
    transition:background .18s ease;
  }
  .tr .clink:hover{background:#FF8A2B}

  .note{
    border-top:1px solid var(--tr-line);padding-top:18px;margin:0;
    font-size:11.5px;color:var(--tr-faint);line-height:1.7;max-width:76ch;
  }

  /* ── responsive ── */
  @media (max-width:1040px){
    .band-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:26px;padding:30px 26px 28px}
    .grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}
  }
  @media (max-width:700px){
    .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .prep{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  }
  @media (max-width:600px){
    .tr-shell{padding:0 16px}
    .band{border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:30px}
    .band-grid{padding:22px 18px 22px}
    .contact{padding:20px}
    .tr .clink{width:100%;text-align:center}
    .cta{width:100%}
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
    .tr *,.tr *::before,.tr *::after{transition-duration:.001ms !important}
  }
</style>
